## Classification

- **Document type:** Empirical–quantitative (primary survey, chi-square/logistic regression), peer-reviewed journal
- **Primary audience:** Academic / BFSI HR and operations practitioners
- **AI explicit:** Yes — survey of AI/ML adoption perceptions among 97 Indian banking employees

## 3–5 Reusable Findings

1. Despite AI's documented benefits, AI-driven technology adoption in Indian banking remains low relative to developed economies — survey-based confirmation of an adoption gap, consistent with [[Governance_Capacity]] framing (feeds S2).
2. KYC automation remains largely manual: 70% of surveyed organisations still use semi-automated KYC (human-involved verification), only 8% use fully automated KYC, and ~24% remain fully human-dependent — a concrete adoption-maturity data point for [[Governance_Debt]] in AI-enabled compliance processes (feeds S2/S6).
3. Significant association (χ²=19.697, p<.01) found between AI/ML adoption and increased customer satisfaction — organisations using AI report measurably better customer-satisfaction outcomes (feeds S2).
4. Significant association (χ²=30.762, p<.01) found between AI/ML adoption and employee-reported data-security/privacy concerns — adoption correlates with heightened internal awareness of data-security risk, a useful empirical anchor for DPDP-readiness arguments (feeds S5/S2).
5. Only 23% of surveyed organisations use fully in-built/proprietary AI mechanisms; 22% rely on third-party AI vendors — evidencing significant third-party/vendor dependency in Indian banking AI deployments, relevant to outsourcing-risk and vendor-governance discussions (feeds S2/S6).

## Consulting / Teaching Reuse

- The KYC automation breakdown (70% semi-automated / 8% fully automated / 24% fully manual) is a ready-made statistic for illustrating the "automation maturity gap" in Indian BFSI AML/KYC compliance — directly usable in AEGIS_OS pitches targeting compliance automation.
- The third-party AI dependency figure (22%) supports vendor-risk-governance discussions with CISOs/COOs.

